1
00:00:49,632 --> 00:00:50,759
I will.

2
00:00:57,348 --> 00:00:58,558
Thank you.

3
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:20,390
Pack all your things.

4
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:31,025
Why did you suddenly disappear?

5
00:02:40,952 --> 00:02:41,870
I only wounded her.

6
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:46,624
You know you only made her angrier.

7
00:03:03,057 --> 00:03:04,309
Your mother was right.

8
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:27,457
Don't worry.

9
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:29,334
I'll handle him.

10
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:35,798
Are you sure?

11
00:03:39,219 --> 00:03:40,053
Like I said,

12
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:47,060
and I'm the only one who can deal with it.

13
00:03:47,143 --> 00:03:49,771
So, I'm the one who'll fix it.

14
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:59,030
It's pretty obvious
the Castellanis are hunting him down.

15
00:04:02,951 --> 00:04:04,452
if he manages to escape with his partner.

16
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:11,292
That might be difficult.

17
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:14,629
Those bastards
are a little too war-hungry.

18
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:20,551
This is a perfect opportunity

19
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:23,554
if the Castellanis will listen to Chiara.

20
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,734
what's your plan?

21
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:46,744
Fix the problem

22
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,080
without making noise.

23
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:10,268
Why haven't we heard anything on comms?

24
00:05:11,227 --> 00:05:12,687
What's happening to Alex?

25
00:05:14,022 --> 00:05:15,398
Lost radio power.

26
00:05:30,204 --> 00:05:31,873
But I don't have a Schengen visa.

27
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:34,667
It takes forever to process,
and we don't have the budget!

28
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:38,671
We have Mikoy's asset there

29
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:39,964
who can help them.

30
00:05:48,806 --> 00:05:50,516
Looks like we can't get out of here.

31
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:58,441
Because they control this area.

32
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:00,693
Even the local police.

33
00:06:04,739 --> 00:06:06,157
We still have one option.

34
00:06:07,825 --> 00:06:10,369
Don't tell me you're counting
on your informant again?

35
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:13,498
He still hasn't let me down
up to now, Alex.

36
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:17,168
You really trust that informant that much.

37
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:19,462
Well, no matter how good he is,

38
00:06:20,671 --> 00:06:22,465
there's no getting past the Castellanis.

39
00:06:23,299 --> 00:06:25,051
Because this isn't just their territory,

40
00:06:25,134 --> 00:06:26,636
it's their kingdom.

41
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:31,349
He's here.

42
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:41,984
You?

43
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:45,655
Come here.

44
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:47,698
You've got some nerve!

45
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:49,408
- What is he doing here?
- Alex, relax!

46
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:53,454
He's just paying for his sins.

47
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:56,332
You have a strong grip, sis.

48
00:06:59,961 --> 00:07:00,962
Rahmboy.

49
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:02,630
The area is on lockdown.

50
00:07:02,713 --> 00:07:04,090
No one's getting out.

51
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:09,011
There's money and gold on your heads.

52
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:11,764
So everyone around here

53
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,599
is looking for the two of you.

54
00:07:15,309 --> 00:07:16,978
So basically, you can't help us?

55
00:07:17,061 --> 00:07:18,062
I didn't say that.

56
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:20,106
Of course I can help you.

57
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:21,232
Come on, you know me.

58
00:07:21,816 --> 00:07:23,484
I owe him big time.

59
00:07:24,777 --> 00:07:25,611
So what?

60
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:28,281
Where are you planning to hide us?

61
00:07:28,906 --> 00:07:30,074
Some kind of animal cage,

62
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,534
or maybe a sewer?

63
00:07:34,245 --> 00:07:37,957
Worse than an animal cage or a sewer, bro.

64
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:42,003
Where?

65
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:05,693
Wait.

66
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:07,153
Why here?

67
00:08:07,778 --> 00:08:09,030
Have you lost your mind?

68
00:08:09,113 --> 00:08:10,364
Do you want us to get killed?

69
00:08:10,865 --> 00:08:12,950
<i>Believe it or not, Sister Alex,</i>

70
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:17,246
How can you say that?

71
00:08:23,794 --> 00:08:25,421
And a five-star place

72
00:08:31,719 --> 00:08:34,263
Because if anything bad happens
to the guests

73
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:36,224
in a high-end place like that…

74
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:40,269
it would be bad for Italy's reputation.

75
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:57,745
The Castellanis won't make a move
inside that five-star hotel.

76
00:09:25,439 --> 00:09:26,691
<i>You know you only made her angrier.</i>

77
00:09:53,467 --> 00:09:54,969
How long are we staying here?

78
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:59,682
look’s like we are not
in Castellani’s radar now.

79
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:03,269
He spread a rumor about us escaping.

80
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:13,404
Seems like that asset of yours
is trustworthy.

81
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:18,117
Wait, I thought we were staying here?

82
00:10:20,953 --> 00:10:23,456
He'll arrange transportation
for us to leave Italy.

83
00:10:32,089 --> 00:10:33,257
Sorry about what?

84
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:37,678
I'm sorry you weren't able to do
what you were supposed to do here.

85
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:42,183
And now, it looks like Chiara
is back in Prague.

86
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:52,568
I have the rest of my life
to hunt her down

87
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:55,363
and make her pay for what she did.

88
00:11:57,842 --> 00:12:00,302
This is how big a ten-peso pandesal is?

89
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:01,554
What is this?

90
00:12:04,598 --> 00:12:07,017
That's fresh from the oven, sweetheart.

91
00:12:08,185 --> 00:12:09,437
I can smell that.

92
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:12,648
Why are you smiling like that?

93
00:12:12,731 --> 00:12:13,732
So damn wide.

94
00:12:15,443 --> 00:12:17,736
It just reminded me of Italy.

95
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:20,698
Do you know the best time in Italy
is in the morning?

96
00:12:21,657 --> 00:12:25,494
Because that's when the city smells like
newly baked bread.

97
00:12:27,163 --> 00:12:28,581
Let's go there, sweetheart!

98
00:12:28,664 --> 00:12:31,125
Then, let's see if they smell even better

99
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:33,002
than the ten-peso pandesal

100
00:12:33,085 --> 00:12:34,587
from Tonyo's Bakery!

101
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:36,255
I think this still smells better.

102
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:42,530
Looks like you don't have a gun
with you now, sweetheart.

103
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:51,747
Because if you did,
I'd be dead by now, right?

104
00:13:54,041 --> 00:13:55,459
Are you sure?

105
00:14:13,727 --> 00:14:15,396
But it won't be quick.

106
00:14:16,355 --> 00:14:17,815
You won't make it easy.

107
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:25,114
You know and I know

108
00:14:26,448 --> 00:14:28,075
that I can be faster than that.

109
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:33,664
All I need is two minutes.

110
00:14:42,339 --> 00:14:44,508
Your jokes with the double meanings.

111
00:14:48,512 --> 00:14:49,847
All I'm saying is

112
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,475
we have another time for this.

113
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:55,936
For now, you have to go back to Alex.

114
00:14:56,478 --> 00:14:58,105
Why? Huh?

115
00:15:00,107 --> 00:15:01,108
What is it this time?!

116
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:04,778
What did you do?

117
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:04,838
HOTEL ELISEO

118
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:28,195
Come on!

119
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:29,196
Let's go.

120
00:16:34,785 --> 00:16:36,954
<i>Please guide me,</i>

121
00:16:37,037 --> 00:16:39,331
<i>especially Chiara.</i>

122
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:42,751
<i>Don't let her heart influence her mind.</i>

123
00:16:43,752 --> 00:16:47,798
<i>This is what was meant to be.</i>
<i>It must be fulfilled.</i>

124
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:06,608
Did something happen?

125
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:16,285
Who? Mother Mary?

126
00:17:17,578 --> 00:17:18,495
Chiara.

127
00:17:21,248 --> 00:17:22,458
What?

128
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:23,751
What happened?

129
00:17:26,628 --> 00:17:28,422
I got close to her.

130
00:17:35,804 --> 00:17:38,098
Are you saying she saved me?

131
00:17:39,433 --> 00:17:40,267
I don't know.

132
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:43,062
All I know is,

133
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:48,901
she would've done it already.

134
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,112
What did she say?

135
00:17:53,822 --> 00:17:55,115
She said we'll face each other.

136
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,290
Looks like she's coming back
to the Philippines.

137
00:18:25,312 --> 00:18:26,313
How did that happen?

138
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:34,530
All this time, there were eyes
watching our every move.

139
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:38,075
So you already know Mikoy's asset?

140
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:40,452
Who is he?

141
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:43,872
More importantly, can we trust him?

142
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:52,631
At least we're sure of his pronouns.

143
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:59,054
But I have to respect Mikoy's request

144
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:01,390
not to reveal his asset's identity.

145
00:19:04,059 --> 00:19:06,812
He doesn't want to violate bro code!

146
00:19:15,571 --> 00:19:18,282
And as for the question
of whether we can trust him,

147
00:19:19,366 --> 00:19:20,492
he saved us.

148
00:19:21,743 --> 00:19:23,662
He had every opportunity

149
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:27,249
to betray us and turn us over
to Chiara and the Concordat,

150
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:29,877
for his own advantage,

151
00:19:30,752 --> 00:19:32,713
but he still chose to help us.

152
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,471
Mikoy's asset can be trusted.

153
00:19:55,903 --> 00:19:58,197
Do you have anything else to say?

154
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:05,579
But she didn't.

155
00:20:07,164 --> 00:20:10,000
Despite knowing we were there
and Mikoy was there to assassinate her.

156
00:20:18,759 --> 00:20:19,885
Or maybe

157
00:20:36,485 --> 00:20:37,903
There are a lot of reasons

158
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:41,406
why Chiara didn't let you die.

159
00:20:50,999 --> 00:20:52,918
she didn't let me die because…

160
00:21:19,903 --> 00:21:21,113
Where's Mikoy?

161
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:26,576
What's that?

162
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,954
I still brought you guys some pasalubong!

163
00:21:29,037 --> 00:21:30,330
This is a promise.

164
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,373
- I want the wafer.
- Sweet!

165
00:21:31,456 --> 00:21:33,125
- There, and then…
- This is wafer.

166
00:21:33,208 --> 00:21:34,042
Perfume!

167
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:34,876
- Hey!
- Hey!

168
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:37,671
Stateside, from Italy!

169
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:39,214
- That's right.
- Spray it in your mouth,

170
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:40,924
- so it'll smell nice for once.
- Captain Pepe.

171
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:42,134
Alcologne.

172
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:44,678
- It tastes like alcohol too!
- No!

173
00:21:44,761 --> 00:21:45,929
It's just perfume.

174
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:46,930
- This one's for you.
- Try it.

175
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:49,599
My most favorite sibling!

176
00:21:49,683 --> 00:21:51,518
- I don't have…
- This is great.

177
00:21:51,601 --> 00:21:52,686
Thank you, bro!

178
00:21:52,769 --> 00:21:54,813
- Seems you have favoritism.
- Something to bring to school.

179
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:59,359
And of course, we must not forget
my dearest mother, right?

180
00:21:59,443 --> 00:22:00,277
- There.
- Of course.

181
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:01,278
Mom!

182
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:05,115
There are some snacks in there, Mom.

183
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:07,117
Those have a lot of sugar, Tess.

184
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:08,118
They're sweet.

185
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:09,953
Son.

186
00:22:10,037 --> 00:22:11,496
Can I talk to you?

187
00:22:13,415 --> 00:22:14,291
Yes, Mom.

188
00:22:30,974 --> 00:22:33,101
Here’s my gift. Open it.

189
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,201
Saikyu.

190
00:22:55,415 --> 00:22:56,291
Shaku.

191
00:23:02,547 --> 00:23:05,467
if you want to slice Mikoy’s neck.

192
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:18,480
You know why I want to eliminate him.

193
00:23:18,563 --> 00:23:21,650
After what happened in Italy,

194
00:23:21,733 --> 00:23:23,902
we can't underestimate him anymore.

195
00:23:28,365 --> 00:23:32,327
And, yes, he failed

196
00:23:32,869 --> 00:23:34,830
when he tried to assassinate you.

197
00:23:34,913 --> 00:23:37,457
But that doesn't mean

198
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:39,501
he won't try again.

199
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:41,545
Maybe next time,

200
00:23:44,172 --> 00:23:45,632
and he'll finally

201
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:47,217
take you down.

202
00:23:52,639 --> 00:23:54,182
Are you underestimating me?

203
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:04,526
That's not what I meant.

204
00:24:12,993 --> 00:24:14,119
But I think

205
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:16,204
you have another reason

206
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:18,915
why you want Mikoy dead so badly.

207
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:32,721
There's another reason
why you want Mikoy gone so badly.

208
00:24:32,804 --> 00:24:34,181
Because you know that

209
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:36,933
if there's one person
in this world I'd listen to, it's him.

210
00:24:50,697 --> 00:24:52,157
<i>I'm sorry, Dad.</i>

211
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:53,783
<i>This is the only way I know.</i>

212
00:24:53,867 --> 00:24:55,035
<i>I'll do whatever it takes</i>

213
00:24:55,118 --> 00:24:56,745
<i>to make whoever did this pay.</i>

214
00:24:56,828 --> 00:24:58,163
You're going to have Chiara killed?

215
00:25:03,293 --> 00:25:05,795
I know you can't
bring yourself to kill Chiara.

216
00:25:05,879 --> 00:25:07,672
I already have another option.

217
00:25:07,756 --> 00:25:10,926
For sure they won't survive tonight.

218
00:25:13,637 --> 00:25:14,596
I'm not your enemy.

219
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:16,848
What's going on here?

220
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:19,476
Lower your guns.

221
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:21,394
He's Mikoy's secret asset.

222
00:25:21,478 --> 00:25:22,687
What is he doing here?

223
00:25:35,867 --> 00:25:38,703
Looks like my sweetheart
still hasn't changed at all.
